    "boss": true,
    "title": "Boss: The Payment Provider Goes Down",
    "from": "Maya, founder of NimbusCart",
    "brief": "Our payment provider just told us they have planned maintenance tonight, right in the dinner rush, and it might run long. I won't turn customers away. Every order must be accepted, every order must be charged eventually, and the queue must be empty by midnight. Build checkout from scratch.",
    "lesson": "Decoupling turns a dependency outage into a delay. Orders are accepted and saved immediately; charges wait in a durable queue and drain once the provider returns.",
